# Deep Jungle (biome: jungle) - 50x50, Amazon river-threaded wilderness
# Tiles: . terra-firme  , varzea  : ruin/plaza paving  S ford  Q deep water
#   walls: # foliage  R Maya ruin  K cliff   trees: V vine-tree  Y palm
#   decor: G fern  O log
# Monsters: o ocelot  j goblin  h huntress  d serpent_dancer  x hexer
#   g gorilla_titan  w orc_hero_boss  i jungle_idol
#
# THE RIVER'S EMBRACE. The Great River comes in at the north edge, and at the
# fork (y7) it SPLITS: the west arm swings wide, the east arm runs straight,
# and between them lies the ISLAND - the whole Lost City stands on it, ringed
# by water. The arms rejoin below the island (y22) and run south out of the
# map. Three crossings only:
#   the WEST BRIDGE (x24-26, y14) - sunken causeway stones to the west gate
#   the EAST BRIDGE (x39-41, y17) - the same, to the east gate
#   the LOWER FORD (x28-30, y40) - the only link between the two banks' varzea
#
# THE LOST CITY (the island, x28-37, y10-19): stone walls, gates west and
# east off the bridges, paved courts. At its heart the ROUND ARENA (x30-35,
# y12-17, gates north and south): the Orc Warlord holds the centre at (32,15)
# and his four warding idols stand around him INSIDE it - (31,13) (34,13)
# (31,16) (34,16) - his ward is map-wide, so breaking it is an in-arena job.
# Hexers and serpent dancers hold the courts; the treasury nook is at (29,11).
#
# WEST BANK
#   The SERPENT GEOGLYPH (x6-15, y2-7): the old paving IS a snake seen from
#     above, and the tome lectern stands on its crown.
#   THE GREAT KAPOK (x3-11, y12-19): one vast tree - a double spiral of
#     trunk-wood; walk in at (11,15), round the coil, and in its heart sit the
#     gorilla titan and a golden hoard.
#   THE OXBOW (x4-11, y24-30): a cut-off loop gone still; a golden hoard on
#     the islet over deep water; a SUNKEN IDOL head on the east trail; one
#     stepping stone (7,24) that walks into the water and stops.
#   The varzea south: the POISON POOL (x14-15, y39-40) steaming in the middle
#     of the flood-forest; a WAYSTONE ruin-fern-ruin at (18-20,35); the
#     LANDING hub at the west wall, where the corridor from the desert opens.
# EAST BANK
#   Thicket country north, a smugglers' cache at (44,6); the MANGROVES south
#   with the STILT PLATFORM (x43-46, y39-43) - sealed, vault the rootwall.
#
# CAPABILITY GATES - rewards only, never a route; Fly clears both.
# gate: water (8,27) chest_golden - the oxbow islet, wants Walk on Water
# gate: jump (44,41) spell_lectern - the stilt platform: stand (42,41), vault
#   the rootwall at (43,41)
